; Run an NPC script command of op 0-3 (a command with objects, or a routine)
;
; Called by the script interpreter (#R$980E) for the ops below SCRIPT_OP_VERB.
; Bit 0 of the command byte tells the two forms apart (the language is described
; at #R$980E). The script pointer (IY+2, IY+3) is first moved past the command
; (#R$9918, length 4).
; .
; Bit 0 clear (ops 0 and 2): CommandId, FirstObject and SecondObject are taken
; from bytes +1 to +3 and the command is tried through #R$99C6 (test pass, then
; done). A refusal is a failure (#R$99AA).
; .
; Bit 0 set (ops 1 and 3): bytes +1 and +2 are the address of a routine, +3 is
; not used. The routine is called like a verb handler in two passes: with
; ActionPerform and ActionAllowed 0 (the test: the routine must set
; ActionAllowed to 1 to agree) and, if it agreed, again with ActionPerform = 1
; (it does its work). A routine that leaves ActionAllowed other than 1 in the
; test is a failure (#R$99AA).
; .
; After a success the NPC is done for this turn. If bit 5 of the command byte
; is set (SCRIPT_BIT_ERASE) the command byte is first set to 0 in the script
; itself (a one-shot command). The other bytes stay, so a script that reaches
; the command again finds op 0 with the old bytes +1 to +3 as verb and objects;
; the only command with this bit in the data is Thorin's routine at $C8FB and
; it has not been seen to be reached again with the inputs in re/maps.
; .
; IX Address of the command (as HL)
; IY The NPC record
@label=RunScriptCommand
c$9928 CALL $9918       ; move the script pointer on
@isub=BIT SCRIPT_BIT_ROUTINE,(IX+$00)
 $992B BIT 0,(IX+$00)   ; a routine?
 $992F JR NZ,$994A      ; yes
 $9931 LD A,(IX+$01)    ; the verb
 $9934 LD ($B6E7),A     ; CommandId
 $9937 LD A,(IX+$02)    ; the first object
 $993A LD ($B6E8),A     ; FirstObject
 $993D LD A,(IX+$03)    ; the second object
 $9940 LD ($B6E9),A     ; SecondObject
 $9943 CALL $99C6       ; try it: Z = refused
 $9946 JR Z,$99AA       ; failed
 $9948 JR $9967         ; done
*$994A LD L,(IX+$01)    ; the routine
 $994D LD H,(IX+$02)
 $9950 SUB A            ; the test pass:
 $9951 LD ($B6FA),A     ; ActionPerform = 0
 $9954 LD ($B6FB),A     ; ActionAllowed = 0
 $9957 CALL $9B6C       ; call it unless it is 0
 $995A LD A,($B6FB)     ; it agreed?
 $995D CP $01
 $995F JR NZ,$99AA      ; no: failed
 $9961 LD ($B6FA),A     ; ActionPerform = 1
 $9964 CALL $9B6C       ; do it
@isub=BIT SCRIPT_BIT_ERASE,(IX+$00)
*$9967 BIT 5,(IX+$00)   ; erase after use?
 $996B JP Z,$9901       ; no: next NPC
 $996E LD (IX+$00),$00
 $9972 JR $9901         ; next NPC
